      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The test method itself is a single chained `EqualsTester` call crammed onto two lines, with many unused data provider methods and all the unused imports from the original larger test class. I'll improve understandability by:\n- Formatting the `INSTANCE` initialization across readable lines\n- Breaking the `EqualsTester` chain into named variables and separate `addEqualityGroup` calls\n- Removing the ~80 unused imports and unused `data_*` provider methods that were copied from the full test classThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused imports and dead `data_*` provider methods, formats the `INSTANCE` builder across readable lines with an explanatory comment, and breaks the `EqualsTester` chain into one `addEqualityGroup` call per line, each annotated with a comment explaining what equality property it is verifying."
